>Pfeifer</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>53BP1 is a positive regulator of the BRCA1 promoter</article-title><source>Cell Cycle</source><year>2005</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>1078</fpage><lpage>1083</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15970701</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perez-Enciso</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>In silico study of transcriptome genetic variation in outbred populations</article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>2004</year><volume>166</volume><fpage>547</fpage><lpage>554</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15020443</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1534/genetics.166.1.547</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zheng</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transcription activity hot spot, is it real or an artifact?</article-title><source>BMC Proc</source><year>2007</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>S94</fpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>